# Cloudflare Pages headers
# Processed by Cloudflare Pages at deploy time — not served as a file.
# Rule matching: Pages MERGES every rule whose path pattern matches a request —
# it does NOT stop at the first match. A file matched by two blocks receives the
# UNION of their headers, and for a header set by both (e.g. Cache-Control) the
# result is order-dependent and effectively undefined for our purposes. The old
# "first match wins" note here was WRONG: it was falsified live during the
# 2026-07-12 council review (Fable head, issue #111) — aladin.wasm matched both
# /assets/js/* (immutable, 1yr) and a /assets/js/aladin.wasm block (max-age
# 86400) and came back with conflicting Cache-Control directives, not the first
# one. The fix was to delete that specific-file block entirely (see the removed
# aladin.wasm rule) and let the versioned filename ride the /assets/js/*
# immutable rule cleanly. Keep every path pattern here non-overlapping.
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/

# ── Security headers (applied to all pages) ──────────────────────────────────
# CSP note — Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon (auto-injected by Pages): the
# script loads from static.cloudflareinsights.com (script-src) and POSTs its
# measurements to cloudflareinsights.com/cdn-cgi/rum (connect-src) — both
# verified from the beacon source 2026-06-10. Allowing only the script host
# would load the beacon but silently block every report. (Comment kept
# OUTSIDE the rule block: Pages docs only document comments between blocks.)
# HSTS (issue #122) — added 2026-08-06 after the council's prerequisite (a
# subdomain HTTPS inventory) was run empirically: CT logs list exactly
# dustin.space, www.dustin.space, and tiles.dustin.space; all three serve
# HTTPS and 301 http->https (tiles' root 404 is R2 having no index object —
# TLS itself is fine). So includeSubDomains is safe. max-age is 6 months —
# meaningful protection without the preload-readiness commitment; `preload`
# is deliberately ABSENT (Chrome's preload list is effectively a one-way
# door and is Dustin's call, not a config default). Note the header only
# rides responses Pages serves (the apex — plus www if it's Pages-served
# rather than a zone-level redirect, which isn't determinable from this
# repo); browsers then apply it to subdomains via includeSubDomains after
# any apex visit — standard HSTS scoping, R2 responses don't need to carry
# it themselves.
# 2026-09-01: live.dustin.space (R2 custom domain, HTTPS) joined the subdomain
# inventory — includeSubDomains still safe.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15768000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://giscus.app https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; worker-src blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://giscus.app; img-src 'self' https://tiles.dustin.space https://live.dustin.space https://cdn.astrobin.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://*.cds.unistra.fr https://*.unistra.fr data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://tiles.dustin.space https://live.dustin.space https://*.cds.unistra.fr https://*.unistra.fr https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src https://giscus.app; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://api.web3forms.com

# Fonts — immutable: content-addressed filenames (woff2 files won't change
# unless the actual font bytes change, at which point the filename changes).
/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Images — long cache, but not immutable (hero/thumbnails may be replaced
# in place without a filename change during early development).
/assets/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Tile pyramids served locally (dev only — production tiles are on R2).
/tiles/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# CSS and JS — long cache, safe because each <link>/<script> URL now
# carries a content-hash query string (?v=<md5-prefix>) generated by
# src/_data/assetHash.js at build time. When a file's content changes,
# its hash changes, the URL changes, and every cache layer (browser +
# Cloudflare edge) treats it as a new resource and fetches fresh.
# When the file is unchanged, the URL is identical and this long cache
# keeps it warm. `immutable` tells well-behaved browsers they never
# need to revalidate the SAME URL — safe under content hashing because
# the URL only repeats when the content does.
/assets/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Covers detail.js/gallery.js (?v= content hash) AND the versioned Aladin
# bundle (aladin-3.8.2.js / aladin-3.8.2.wasm). All three are safe under
# immutable: the JS carries a ?v= hash and the Aladin filenames carry the
# version, so a content change always changes the URL. No aladin.wasm-specific
# block here anymore — it overlapped this rule and produced conflicting
# Cache-Control directives (see the header note at the top of this file).
/assets/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
